{"id": "EUVD-2026-91464", "enisaUuid": "28dd6721-3f1a-3351-b3c7-110c517234bd", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains a cross-site request forgery vulnerability in the admintag action that allows attackers to delete tag associations by luring administrators to crafted GET links. Attackers can supply a wide id range in the delete_tag parameter via top-level navigation, carrying the SameSite=Lax admin cookie, to bulk-delete tag triples.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T16:15:37", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-5c27-6gcm-hc7x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-csrf-tag-deletion-via-admintag-action"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104453", "GHSA-x3mc-2q4x-cvvm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8897caca-77c5-3a1e-bf4c-4c221f5f9db4", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "46fc0aad-997f-3c2d-a26a-a8d183aa9398", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}